' bug-556: a list literal written INLINE at a call argument used to lower as
' `List OF Unknown`, whatever its elements were.
'
' `check_builtin_comparability` deliberately lets an `Unknown` element pass — it
' must never reject on a type it cannot see — so the rule was silently skipped
' for the inline spelling. The same list given a NAME first inferred `List OF Bag`
' and was refused. The verdict depended on whether the author had bound the list,
' not on the types, which is what makes this a silently-skipped rule rather than
' a missing one.
'
' All FOUR call sites below must be refused. Two of them (11, 14) were already
' refused before the fix; the pair on 9 and 12 is the regression under test, and
' keeping all four in one fixture is what pins that the two spellings AGREE
' rather than merely that the inline one now fails.
IMPORT collections

TYPE Bag
  items AS List OF Integer
END TYPE

FUNC main AS Integer
  LET one AS Bag = Bag[[1, 2]]
  LET a AS Integer = collections::find([one], one)
  LET inferred = [one]
  LET b AS Integer = collections::find(inferred, one)
  LET c AS Boolean = collections::contains([one], one)
  LET annotated AS List OF Bag = [one]
  LET d AS Integer = collections::find(annotated, one)
  RETURN a + b + d
END FUNC
